  "reasoning": "The testimony of the tea‑stall owner (PW‑2) shows the accused entered the shop after closing, and the only key that could open the drawer was in the storeroom where staff could reach it. No evidence shows the accused had honest intent or that the cash was recovered. The confession is inadmissible under BSA‑23, but the circumstantial chain is complete.",
  "legal_standard_applied": "The prosecution must prove every element of the offence beyond reasonable doubt.",
