}

{
  "reasoning": "The prosecution relies solely on circumstantial evidence: one witness (PW‑2) placing the accused at the shop, and the complainant’s testimony (PW‑1) that the accused left the shop earlier. A conflicting alibi (DW‑1) is unverified and not corroborated. No confession or physical proof links the accused to the theft, leaving reasonable doubt.",
  "legal_standard_applied": "The prosecution must prove each element of theft beyond a reasonable doubt; any lingering doubt requires acquittal.",
